  "notes": "Staging v4 (v2b): 18:54 and 18:56 are stage scenes in a town: three faceless disbelievers (3 figures = a group) dispute among themselves (speak, inside the group), shake their heads at the truth (54:14, 56:13) and turn away in mockery (56:16); the book plate marks the Quran (54:5) and His verses (56:15), the burst plate the glad tidings (56:5; it leaves when the dispute begins, 56:7). The messengers are never drawn and no pan drifts toward an empty side on «المرسلين». 18:55 (the threat) stays a calm ambient night sky with the lamp and lightning plates. v2: the lamp plate now covers 55:7-8 and leaves before the Name (55:10); no sparkle on the Name and no sky tilt just before it. The clouds parting on 55:7 became birds: its rays from above would still shine on the Name (55:10). v2b: c1 and c3 restaged as above; c2 mood night_sky instead of dawn (no dawn over the threat of 55:14-19), with stars instead of birds at 55:7; the gloss on 54:2 has no arrow, the glosses on 54:14 and 56:11 point at the disputers."
